---

**Step 1: Find the number of mystery books.**  
Nancy has **2 shelves** of mystery books, and each shelf holds **6 books**.  
So, the number of mystery books is:  
$$
2 \text{ shelves} \times 6 \text{ books/shelf} = 12 \text{ books}
$$

---

