Nancy has **6 shelves** of picture books, and each shelf also holds **6 books**.  
So, the number of picture books is:  
$$
6 \text{ shelves} \times 6 \text{ books/shelf} = 36 \text{ books}
$$

---

**Step 3: Add the mystery and picture books to find the total.**  
$$
12 \text{ mystery books} + 36 \text{ picture books} = 48 \text{ books}
$$

